4ebb86e19737b90ca861f84e42e2d9e4c6","event_uuid":"6ad2ddcf-fa50-4cfa-9229-7898fa908959","position":{"commit_sha":"c114d8fe437cf4af682b17d0045b426372dd0354","position":"1792375580510240810-6ad2ddcf-fa50-4cfa-9229-7898fa908959"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"83259ac9b1fe85bb34538f3d8a786d4198e9ca56b86a4d5f054d90125e3e8042","event_uuid":"02974c3e-a470-4cb7-acc3-0d99143e1fc6","position":{"commit_sha":"9fae9e0aaa459c13f2d77b7e59d13fc6c66f016b","position":"1792377764255860132-02974c3e-a470-4cb7-acc3-0d99143e1fc6"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"7814cb065a303545ea7db3ff7188271a7eb209ff7ec0b9660c4bee94459313f6","event_uuid":"6a2adf7a-6cbf-432e-a32c-49f8ce87bab5","position":{"commit_sha":"481051455620ff43a3960abb3ebd1cc9ba85c297","position":"1792377989212115111-6a2adf7a-6cbf-432e-a32c-49f8ce87bab5"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"acce8bcca5e362eca91d93a36e825cde75b5a107eab49aaf38827b2225526a4d","event_uuid":"e21dcd63-40c9-4284-aefc-7b3792829fdf","position":{"commit_sha":"bd51a9134c769282a7eae97a91b435de069d79b9","position":"1792378009503872225-e21dcd63-40c9-4284-aefc-7b3792829fdf"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"regression","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause W1 confirmed and fixed in the worktree (fix-3b27-stale-review, base 3beb7e4ad23).\n\nEvidence: in-process repro with no LLM — begin_gate_job, edit_ticket, begin_gate_job -> is_new=False and the same job_id, while show_ticket already returned the edited text. Tool-level red: the 2 new tests in tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py failed on the base (review_plan_start returned the same job id; sync review_plan ran the gate 1 time instead of 2, sharing the stale run).\n\nFix: _mcp_llm._plan_review_variant adds `material=<current plan-material fingerprint>` (attest.current_material_fingerprint, a light read) to the dedup variant at both plan-review call sites; the async start computes it in the worker thread, not on the event loop. Unchanged material still dedups (existing tests pass). 43 passed across test_mcp_llm_dedup, test_mcp_inflight, test_mcp_gate_async. make lint and make typecheck pass; make verify running.\n\nW2 (cross-clone 60 s fetch throttle) is tracked in glandulous-minor-aurochs. Side observation while working this ticket: I edited this description from a local clone and waited 90 s before review_plan_start; the resulting REVIEW_RESULT pins description hash 52943bbb44fe9393 (5716 chars), equal to the current description.","timestamp":1792372103643016173},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed: Gerrit 3040, PS2 LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, 0 unresolved; submitted at revision 0b4062cbbbac; merged on main as 864b6f56c91 (server rebase over 21dabcbb2c1). PS2 corrected the _plan_review_variant docstring (an unreadable fingerprint yields the literal `material=None` key) and added a variant-level test. make verify on the fix: 17 failed / 20352 passed, all 17 the known arm64 pandoc `Bad CPU type` host defect (frenzied-snively-llama), nothing else. First push attempt was rejected `remote unpack failed: Missing tree 96cc404c1cb` (tree of 08033c6ae93, an ancestor of HEAD already on Gerrit as refs/changes/42/2742/2); the identical push succeeded on retry, consistent with a transient server object-store fault. Advisory left as-is: current_material_fingerprint_impl re-raises only while a pinned completion view is bound, which the MCP tool entry points never bind.","timestamp":1792377764255860132}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1789974996285635071,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ff66603e-0df2-41de-a355-cb0f0623e6c4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"35b7-e00c-e16b-4faa"},{"link_uuid":"6ad2ddcf-fa50-4cfa-9229-7898fa908959","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"fb1d-ab39-f00f-4385"}],"description":"## Symptom\n\nRunning plan review through the MCP server (`review_plan_start` / `review_plan`) can\nreview a **stale copy of the ticket description** instead of the current one. After\nediting a ticket's description to address blocking findings, a fresh MCP review returned\n**byte-identical findings** -- including findings whose text had already been removed\nfrom the plan -- and recorded a `material_parts.description` fingerprint matching the\npre-edit description rather than the edited one.\n\nRunning `rebar review-plan <id>` from a local worktree immediately afterwards, with no\nother change, read the current description and produced different (correct) findings.\n\n## Why this is serious\n\nPlan review is a **gate that mints a signed attestation**, and the attestation's whole\nvalue is that it binds a verdict to specific pinned material. If the material the MCP\npath pins is not the material in the store, then:\n\n- A plan can be BLOCKED for findings the author has already fixed, with no way to clear\n  them through the MCP path -- the author edits, re-reviews, and gets the same verdict.\n- More dangerously, the inverse: a plan can be PASSED and certified against a description\n  that is no longer what the ticket says.\n\n`AGENTS.md` instructs agents to route tracker operations, explicitly including\n`review-plan`, through the MCP server when one is configured. So the documented default\npath is the affected one, and the working path (local CLI) is documented as the fallback.\n\n## Evidence\n\nObserved in session `cd818479-c2e0-4a67-a07f-2d230e321466` on more than one ticket. The\ntell is the `material_fingerprint` / `material_parts.description` in the review result:\ncompare it against a fingerprint computed from the description that `show_ticket` returns\nat the same moment. When they disagree, the review ran on stale material.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed 2026-10-18, origin/main 3beb7e4ad23)\n\nTwo independent windows exist. Only W1 is fixed here; W2 is split out.\n\n**W1 — dedup attaches a post-edit start to a pre-edit run (fixed here).** The MCP singleflight\nkey (`src/rebar/_mcp_inflight.py` `compute_key`) hashes gate, canonical ticket id, code basis\nSHA, variant, and readonly flag. Plan material is not in it. Both plan-review call sites in\n`src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` (`review_plan_start` ~line 258, sync `review_plan` ~line 445) pass\n`variant=f\"source={source or 'attested'}\"`. So while a review of ticket T is in flight, an\nedit to T followed by a new start returns the SAME job, whose material was snapshotted at its\nown start. The caller then polls byte-identical findings pinned to the pre-edit description —\nthe reported symptom. Window: the remaining lifetime of the in-flight run (a review takes 15\nto 20 minutes); the key is purged when the run completes, so a start after completion is fresh.\n\nReproduced in-process with no LLM: `begin_gate_job` on a fresh ticket, `edit_ticket` the\ndescription, `begin_gate_job` again -> `is_new=False`, same `job_id`, while `show_ticket`\nalready returns the edited text.\n\nSigning is NOT the hole for a same-store edit: `generation.sign_manifest` re-collects the\nmaterial under the store lock and raises `PlanReviewGenerationChanged` when the ticket's own\nmaterial moved, so the attached run cannot sign over the edit. The defect is that the edited\nplan never gets reviewed through the start the author issued after editing.\n\n**W2 — cross-clone replication lag (out of scope; follow-up ticket).** The server reads its\nown tickets clone; an edit made in another clone reaches it only through\n`reads.ensure_fresh`, a `git fetch` throttled to once per 60 s. A review started within 60 s\nof the server's previous fetch reads the pre-edit copy. Fixing this changes the shared\nread-freshness/locking path and is tracked separately.\n\nForensic check of this repo's tracker: 4210 REVIEW_RESULT events compared against the\ndescription current at each review's timestamp. No result pins a description older than the\none current when its run started; the one review whose pin predates an edit (326f-595a,\n2026-08-27 17:11 PDT, BLOCK, unsigned) had the edit land during the run.\n\n## Plan\n\n1. Add `_plan_review_variant(ticket_id, source)` in `src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py` returning\n   `f\"source={source or 'attested'};material={fp}\"`, where `fp` is\n   `rebar.llm.plan_review.attest.current_material_fingerprint(ticket_id)` (a light read, no\n   LLM; returns None on a read failure, which keeps the old key behaviour for that call).\n2. Use it at both plan-review call sites. `_mcp_inflight.py` is unchanged: material enters\n   through the existing `variant` dimension.\n3. `verify_completion` dedup is unchanged here (the ticket is about plan review).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Regression test in `tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py`: on a real temp store, a blocked\n      `review_plan_start` run is in flight, the description is edited, and a second\n      `review_plan_start` returns a NEW job whose gate call happens after the edit. The test\n      fails on origin/main (same job id returned) and passes with the fix.\n- [x] Same check through the sync `review_plan` tool: after an edit, a concurrent call runs\n      the gate a second time instead of sharing the first result.\n- [x] Unchanged material still de-duplicates: the existing\n      `test_two_concurrent_calls_invoke_the_gate_exactly_once` cases pass unchanged.\n- [x] The dedup key incorporates the material fingerprint (asserted by the tests above).\n- [x] A follow-up ticket for W2 exists, linked `discovered_from` this ticket.\n\n## Testing\n\n```\n.venv/bin/pytest tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py tests/unit/test_mcp_inflight.py tests/unit/test_mcp_gate_async.py -p no:randomly -q\nmake lint && make typecheck && make verify\n```\n","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_mcp_llm.py","reason":"plan-review dedup variant at review_plan_start and sync review_plan includes the ticket's current plan-material fingerprint"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_llm_dedup.py","reason":"regression oracle: an edit while a review is in flight makes the next start/call run a fresh gate; unchanged material still dedups"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","managed_refs":[["relates_to","35b7-e00c-e16b-4faa"],["relates_to","fb1d-ab39-f00f-4385"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"6a2adf7a-6cbf-432e-a32c-49f8ce87bab5","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["mcp","plan-review","gate-integrity"],"ticket_id":"3b27-8f4b-90bd-44b2","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP plan-review can review and attest against a stale ticket description","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7227c8bd-394f-4b92-bbbb-069d61756301","dc39d790-d44e-49bf-ad81-57713b0c1ce6","ef314bb8-ed9b-4d30-b98e-ae6d567e5979","ee183fa9-3d94-42c6-8401-5d15fdf03f3b","cfc6c9ed-5306-42a3-840d-6a10ff0df29b","3de85e05-0ba2-4e87-8ff0-a116e4d3b7f7","ff66603e-0df2-41de-a355-cb0f0623e6c4","6ad2ddcf-fa50-4cfa-9229-7898fa908959","9aa0e499-5b6e-4322-a6df-84ddd4b18d51","02974c3e-a470-4cb7-acc3-0d99143e1fc6","6a2adf7a-6cbf-432e-a32c-49f8ce87bab5","e21dcd63-40c9-4284-aefc-7b3792829fdf"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1792380017263986001,"uuid":"3a929632-2c1e-4910-99fd-1d074a6fc550"}